@* A container's own verbs: start or stop, restart, the menu and remove, the
   group the Containers list's card keeps at the right end of its actions row,
   standing alone. Its shortcuts are an object of their own (ContainerShortcuts),
   so the user places each; its menu is
   therefore the whole list, as a table row's is, since the shortcuts may not
   be on the dashboard at all. A verb that changes the container reads the
   list again at once, so every object of the container shows the change. It
   fills its cells with the row's tone and stands at the right, until another
   alignment is chosen. In design the canvas makes it inert. *@
@namespace WslcAgent.UI.Dashboard.Objects
@using Berpiztu.Dashboard.Catalogue
@using Berpiztu.Dashboard.Model
@inherits ContainerObject
@attribute [DashboardObject("wslc.container-verbs", "Container verbs", Group = "Container", Subgroup = "User", Icon = Icons.Material.Filled.SmartButton, Source = ContainerSourceFamily.FamilyKey, Columns = 8, Rows = 2, Fills = true, Background = ThemeColor.PrimaryTint, Horizontal = HorizontalAlign.Right, Anchor = Berpiztu.Dashboard.Model.HorizontalAnchor.Both)]

@if (Container is { } c)
{
    <div class="@SectionClass()">
        <EntityCardPart>
            <MudCardActions Class="py-1" Style="@CardTone.Style(CardTone.Of(c))">
                <VerbTaps>
                    <ContainerActions Container="c" Changed="@(() => Containers.RefreshAsync())" />
                </VerbTaps>
            </MudCardActions>
        </EntityCardPart>
    </div>
}
